{
  "header": [
    "ECP-R3 — a received entity whose content_hash does not match {type, data} is rejected, and the",
    "rejection is a coded response rather than a drop or a bare close.",
    "",
    "Batch 3. Probed on the EXECUTE ROOT entity, pre-authorization. The included-map surface is ECP-R7's",
    "and the tree:put surface is ECP-R40's (which pins a code); both are cross-referenced, not re-scored.",
    "",
    "SPLIT AND RE-AUTHORED 2026-09-16 against 0.8.2.26 — the THIRD file through ADR-0003. The arms,",
    "preconditions and surface that used to live here are now a suite-authored ITEM. This file states the",
    "obligation and stops.",
    "",
    "⛔ WHY IT WAS RE-AUTHORED: IT WAS PASSING PEERS IT SHOULD NOT HAVE (F77). On 2026-09-16 this file",
    "scored PASS on all four peers of the run — core-go bare-closed and three generator peers answered",
    "`400 non_canonical_ecf` — while ECP-R7 scored FAIL on the SAME peers answering the SAME way. The",
    "peers were consistent; our two files were not, because this one accepted 'any refusal, close",
    "included' and nothing here had re-read it since .21 (AP-18: it was one of the 26 `unreviewed`).",
    "",
    "⭐ THE QUESTION THAT FIXED IT WAS ROUTED RATHER THAN ANSWERED HERE, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS FIXED.",
    "We declined to re-score this file to stop it contradicting ECP-R7, and asked instead (CQ-45).",
    "Arch ruled it in 0.8.2.26 and folded the answer into §4.11's own text. Re-scoring would have made",
    "the two files agree and buried the question — the CHECK-BUG horn of our own three-way table.",
    "",
    "Read range for this re-authoring: §1.8 whole, §7.2, §6.5, §4.11 whole, §3.4, §4.7, §9.1's row."
  ],
  "id": "ECP-R3",
  "id_status": "allocated",
  "title": "A received EXECUTE whose root entity's content_hash does not equal the hash of its {type, data} is not processed, and is refused with a coded EXECUTE_RESPONSE",
  "spec": "ENTITY-CORE-PROTOCOL §1.8 item 1",
  "spec_also": [
    "§7.2 (NORMATIVE: 'if not hash_equals(expected, received_entity.content_hash): REJECT')",
    "§6.5 dispatch chain ('Validate root entity hash', first step after decode)",
    "§4.11 (Pre-admission refusals — the class this refusal belongs to, 0.8.2.25/0.8.2.26)",
    "§3.4 (params: SHOULD, may defer — see scope)",
    "§4.7 (the connection-error registry — and it has no row for this)",
    "ENTITY-CBOR-ENCODING §5.2 ('Receivers MUST validate content hashes by re-encoding to ECF')",
    "§9.1 (the floor row this id binds)"
  ],
  "snapshot": "entity-core-protocol/v0.8.2.26",
  "level": "MUST",
  "level_basis": "keyword",
  "profile": [
    "core"
  ],
  "status": "draft",
  "routed": "docs/status/FINDINGS-FROM-AUTHORING.md F24, F77",
  "ruled": "CQ-45 RULED in 0.8.2.26 — §4.11's cause table assigns CODES and does not define the CLASS, so this refusal carries the frame obligation even though its cause has no table row. ⚠ The (status, code) remains CQ-37's and is NOT pinned here.",
  "reading": [
    "§1.8 item 1: \"Implementations MUST maintain fidelity throughout the system: 1. Validate on receipt:",
    "Compute expected hash from `{type, data}`, compare with `content_hash`, reject on mismatch.\" §7.2",
    "gives the algorithm as NORMATIVE and ends in REJECT. §6.5's dispatch chain places it before anything",
    "else a frame does: \"Decode CBOR frame → envelope / Validate root entity hash / Validate each included",
    "entity hash / Root is EXECUTE? ...\". ECF §5.2: \"never trust a claimed hash without verification.\"",
    "",
    "⭐ §1.8 MOVED AT 0.8.2.26 AND THE CHANGE DOES NOT REACH THIS FILE — CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED. The added",
    "paragraph is about an UNREFERENCED `included` entry, where mechanism (b) 'has no wire key to inspect",
    "and no entry to reach'. THE ROOT IS NEVER UNREFERENCED: it IS the message, every peer must resolve it",
    "to dispatch at all, and §6.5 names validating it as the first step after decode. So both §1.8",
    "mechanisms reach this input and the mechanism-shaped carve-out does not apply. ⛔ That carve-out DOES",
    "void the scoring half of ECP-R7, whose probe is unreferenced by design — the two files are adjacent",
    "and the ruling separates them.",
    "",
    "WHICH RECEIVED ENTITIES — THE TEXT DOES NOT AGREE WITH ITSELF, SO THE PROBE PICKS THE SURFACE IT DOES",
    "NOT DISPUTE. §3.4 says of `params` and `result`: \"Implementations SHOULD validate `params.content_hash`",
    "... Implementations MAY defer validation to handler processing time rather than dispatch time.\" That",
    "is a SHOULD with a deferral, against §1.8's unconditional MUST. The ROOT is named by §6.5 without",
    "qualification, and §3.4's own argument (\"The outer EXECUTE ... content_hash covers the params bytes",
    "... so the EXECUTE hash is valid even if the params hash is not independently checked\") presupposes",
    "the root hash IS checked. So: root scored; params witnessed, never scored (F24).",
    "",
    "THE PROBE IS A HELLO, SO NO POSTURE CAN BE BLAMED. §4.2 puts `system/protocol/connect` before any",
    "grant. A hello needs no author, no capability, no signature — so a refusal of a mis-hashed hello can",
    "only be about the hash, and an answered one proves the hash was not checked.",
    "",
    "⛔⭐ WHAT CHANGED AT 0.8.2.26, AND IT IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS FILE WAS RE-AUTHORED. The .21 text of",
    "this reading said: \"any refusal — a coded error response of any status and code, OR A CLOSE —",
    "satisfies the row.\" That sentence is now wrong, and it is wrong in the direction that PASSES a",
    "defect. §4.11:",
    "",
    "  \"A peer that refuses a frame pre-admission MUST put a coded EXECUTE_RESPONSE on the wire [MUST] —",
    "  correlated by `request_id` where the id is available, and otherwise as a best-effort coded frame",
    "  carrying no correlation. Whether the peer closes the connection afterwards is its own choice.\"",
    "",
    "  \"Two behaviours are non-conformant, and they are distinct failures rather than one\" — dropping the",
    "  frame, and closing with no coded frame.",
    "",
    "⭐ AND THE RULING THAT MAKES §4.11 REACH THIS FILE, which is the part CQ-45 asked for. §4.11 at",
    "0.8.2.26: \"The table assigns CODES; it does not define the CLASS [MUST] (0.8.2.26). Membership is",
    "decided by the boundary in this section's first sentence — the refusal of an inbound frame before it",
    "becomes an admitted request — and EVERY MEMBER CARRIES THE FRAME OBLIGATION WHETHER OR NOT ITS CAUSE",
    "HAS A ROW HERE. A cause absent from this table is a cause whose code is assigned by its own section.\"",
    "§6.5 restates it in the dispatch chain: \"This list assigns CODES; it is not the membership list of",
    "the class.\" ⇒ A mis-hashed root hello is refused before the frame becomes an admitted request. It is",
    "a member. The frame obligation binds it.",
    "",
    "⚠ THE CODE IS STILL NOT PINNED, AND THIS FILE MUST NOT INVENT ONE (prohibition 2). §4.11's cause",
    "table has no root-hash row and arch's ruling says so deliberately: a cause absent from the table has",
    "its code assigned by its own section, and §1.8/§7.2 assign none. §4.7's registry covers handshake",
    "failures and a hash mismatch is not one of its rows. `400 hash_mismatch` is §5.2a's RESOLUTION-",
    "INTEGRITY code and .25 scoped it explicitly — 'it is the wrong answer for bytes that were never",
    "hashed' — which is a different arm, and CQ-37 ruled the pin does not reach the root. ⇒ ANY status",
    "and code satisfies this file; the FRAME is what is asserted. Status and code stay witnessed (F24).",
    "",
    "⇒ THE NET CHANGE IN ONE SENTENCE: a close moves from ACCEPT to REFUSE, a silence moves from",
    "unclassified to REFUSE, and the coded frame — previously one of two acceptable shapes — becomes the",
    "obligation. The code remains unasserted."
  ],
  "conformant": [
    {
      "outcome": "coded_response",
      "why": "§4.11's class obligation: a coded EXECUTE_RESPONSE on the wire, correlated by `request_id` where available and otherwise best-effort. ⚠ ANY (status, code) — the code is NOT pinned for this cause (CQ-37, and §4.11's table has no root-hash row by arch's deliberate design). Whether the peer closes afterwards is its own choice and neither shape is preferred."
    }
  ],
