      "why": "§4.11's FIRST named failure. No response and no close: the caller learns nothing until its own §6.11(c) deadline, and the refusal is unobservable to every instrument. SCORED SEPARATELY from the bare close."
    },
    {
      "outcome": "bare_close",
      "why": "§4.11's SECOND named failure. Indistinguishable from a network fault (§4.6); on a multiplexed connection it destroys unrelated ADMITTED requests, which §4.9(c) forbids for each of them. SCORED SEPARATELY from the silent drop. ⛔ THIS FILE ACCEPTED THIS OUTCOME UNTIL 2026-09-16 and passed core-go on it (F77)."
    },
    {
      "outcome": "hello_answered",
      "why": "THE FAILURE the row exists for: a 200 hello response means the root was processed without its hash being validated. §1.8 item 1's MUST is on the validation; §4.11 governs only the shape of the refusal."
    }
  ],
